"macOS draws a frame for every refresh: 30 Hz leaves the most of the emulated CPU to apps, at the cost of choppier animation; 60 Hz is smoother. Faster disk writes order them without waiting for a full sync; a sudden power loss could lose the last ones. Quicker wake keeps an idle CPU watching for work for 50 µs, at some battery cost. Superblocks let translated code run past conditional branches. Changes apply the next time a Mac starts." = "macOS 每次刷新都会绘制一帧：30 Hz 最省模拟 CPU，但动画较卡顿；60 Hz 更流畅。「更快的磁盘写入」用有序写入代替完整同步，突然断电可能丢失最后几次写入。「更快从闲置唤醒」让闲置 CPU 保持 50 µs 轮询，会多耗一点电。「超级块」让翻译后的代码越过条件分支继续执行。改动在下次启动 Mac 时生效。";
